# XALT local test install on Delta (NCSA)

Last updated: 2026 August. Tested on Delta login nodes (`dt-login*`).

Start on a **new machine** with an empty directory. Clone the XALT repo from GitHub,
apply the edits below **once**, build, then run Python test scripts. JSON records land
under `PREFIX_DIR/log_repo/`. Python `pkg.*` records are restricted to package names
your script (or interactive line) **literally imports** — via AST parse, not stack walking.

---

- **`PREFIX_DIR`** is your install root, e.g. `/u/you/ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00`.
- **`XALT_REPO`** is the git URL you clone (e.g. `https://github.com/ncsa/xalt.git`).

---

## Directory layout (when finished)

```
PREFIX_DIR/
  target/                          ← XALT_BASE_DIRECTORY
    xalt2/
      xalt_src/                    ← build source (second clone, created by build)
      xalt/xalt/                   ← installed binaries + site_packages
      module/xalt/3.0.2.lua        ← generated at build (from your template)
  log_repo/delta/json/YYYYMM/      ← JSON output at runtime
  xalt/                            ← your git clone (you edit files here)
```

---

## Step 1 — Create `PREFIX_DIR` and clone XALT

  export PREFIX_DIR=/path/to/ncsa_xalt_test_versions/00
  export XALT_REPO=https://github.com/ncsa/xalt.git

  mkdir -p $PREFIX_DIR
  cd $PREFIX_DIR
  git clone $XALT_REPO xalt

  mkdir -p target
  export XALT_BASE_DIRECTORY=$PREFIX_DIR/target

Use your fork or branch if your team maintains one (e.g. `git clone -b hung ...`).

